## 🚧 3. Core Interface States

The system handles student inputs using four distinct interface states to keep user loops tight and direct.

### A. Initialization State
The system pulls data from the database and updates the progress displays.
*   *UI Presentation:* Renders clear conceptual unit labels and lists the target point criteria derived from the official rubrics. The input workspaces display faded placeholder text tracking the structural parameters required for each step.

### B. Input Validation & Verification State
The engine evaluates live keystroke metrics against structural limits.
*   *UI Presentation:* Displays a neutral loading animation while the text is sent to the backend endpoint. Character count trackers change color dynamically to indicate if an entry is within bounds.

### C. Remediation Intercept State
Triggered when the backend engine flags an omit error via the **Logic-Gap Protocol**.
*   *UI Presentation:* Highlights skipped steps in the text string using the visual bracket marker (`[...]`). The system displays an inline sub-challenge card containing targeted hints, while locking primary dashboard navigation until the response is updated.

### D. Verification Log State
Triggered once the text response clears the evaluation layer and scores points.
*   *UI Presentation:* Displays green checkmarks next to completed steps and registers the points on the scoreboard. It presents an analytical comparison block comparing the student's entry directly with verified rubric definitions, and unlocks the next study block.
